# Customer Behaviour Analysis

An end-to-end Data Analytics project focused on understanding customer shopping patterns, product preferences, purchasing behaviour, discounts, subscriptions, and customer loyalty using **Python, MySQL, and Power BI**.

---

## 📌 Project Overview

This project analyses **3,900 customer purchase records** to understand shopping behaviour and identify meaningful business insights.

The project follows an end-to-end data analytics workflow, including data cleaning and exploratory data analysis using Python, business-focused SQL querying using MySQL, and interactive dashboard development using Power BI.

## 🎯 Project Objectives

- Understand customer demographics and purchasing patterns.
- Compare revenue and spending across different customer groups.
- Examine subscription behaviour and repeat purchases.
- Identify popular, highly rated, and discount-dependent products.
- Analyse shipping methods and their relationship with purchase amounts.
- Present key metrics and trends through an interactive Power BI dashboard.

---

## 📂 Dataset Description

The dataset contains **3,900 rows and 18 columns**.

| Category | Fields |
|:---|:---|
| Customer Demographics | Age, Gender, Location, Subscription Status |
| Purchase Details | Item Purchased, Category, Purchase Amount, Season, Size, Color |
| Shopping Behaviour | Discount Applied, Previous Purchases, Frequency of Purchases |
| Customer Feedback & Fulfilment | Review Rating, Shipping Type |

**Data Quality & Cleaning:**

- The original dataset contained 37 missing values in the `Review Rating` column.
- Missing values were imputed using the median review rating within each product category.

> Note: The original dataset is not included in this repository. Ensure you have permission before publishing any source data.

